## How Has This Been Tested?

- Unit tests in `tests/unit/test_context.py` cover the auth code path and what's passed to
  it, arguments, `Path` input, registering once, timeout, a failed sign-in, refusing someone
  else, broker fallback, siblings, and rejected inputs.
- `tests/integration/test_chosen_browser.py` runs the real MSAL and a real launched stand-in
  browser (`tests/integration/fake_browser.py`): the program gets its arguments with the
  address last, the code is redeemed, and an answer with the wrong state is refused.
- `tests/live/test_sign_in.py::test_interactive_login_in_a_chosen_browser` passed against a
  real tenant, opening in Edge, both plain and with `--profile-directory`. It runs when
  `AZURE_AUTH_TEST_BROWSER` is set (see `.env.example`).
- The pre-push suite (510 tests), ruff and mypy pass.

